QB[2]=[
["Operator-driven reliability (ODR) is best described as:","Operators detect problems early, fix minor ones, and get major ones repaired in a planned way","Operators take over the PM tasks so that maintenance can focus on breakdowns and projects","Operators record downtime so reliability engineers can analyze production losses","Maintenance technicians operate the equipment during off-shifts to learn the process","Operator-driven reliability (ODR) menjadikan operator bagian dari asset care. Operator memantau kesehatan aset (kebocoran, suara, suhu, getaran), memperbaiki penyimpangan kecil sendiri (membersihkan, mengencangkan, melumasi), dan meminta perbaikan besar kepada maintenance secara terencana. ODR juga disebut OBR, OBM, atau TPM.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Operator mengambil alih PM agar maintenance fokus pada breakdown: tujuannya justru mengurangi breakdown, bukan memindahkan beban.\n• Operator mencatat downtime saja: pencatatan hanyalah sebagian kecil dari peran ODR.\n• Teknisi mengoperasikan mesin: arah perannya terbalik.",7],
["Total productive maintenance (TPM) was first developed in the:","1960s in Japan","1950s in the United States","1970s in Germany","1980s in Japan","TPM berakar pada pengenalan preventive maintenance di Jepang pada tahun 1960-an. Nippondenso adalah perusahaan pertama yang menerapkan PM menyeluruh pada 1960, lalu menambahkan autonomous maintenance oleh operator.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• 1950-an di AS: PM ala Amerika memang diadopsi Jepang, tetapi konsep TPM lahir di Jepang.\n• 1970-an di Jerman: tidak terkait.\n• 1980-an di Jepang: saat itu TPM sudah berkembang dan mulai menyebar ke Barat.",7],
["Which company was the first to obtain TPM certification?","Nippondenso","Toyota Motor","Nissan","Mitsubishi Heavy Industries","Nippondenso, pemasok part dari grup Toyota, adalah perusahaan pertama yang memperoleh sertifikasi TPM (Distinguished Plant Prize dari JIPE).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Toyota Motor: terkenal dengan Toyota Production System (lean), bukan sertifikasi TPM pertama.\n• Nissan dan Mitsubishi Heavy Industries: tidak tercatat sebagai yang pertama.",7],
["Who led the effort that named the concept total productive maintenance?","Seiichi Nakajima","Taiichi Ohno","Shigeo Shingo","Kaoru Ishikawa","Seiichi Nakajima dari Japan Institute of Plant Engineers (JIPE, kini JIPM) memimpin upaya ini dan memberi nama 'total productive maintenance', karena seluruh ('total') karyawan terlibat.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Taiichi Ohno: bapak Toyota Production System (JIT, kanban).\n• Shigeo Shingo: SMED dan poka-yoke.\n• Kaoru Ishikawa: diagram fishbone dan quality circle.",7],
["The goals of TPM include:","Zero defects, zero breakdowns, and zero accidents","Zero inventory, zero defects, and zero waiting","Zero breakdowns, zero overtime, and zero backlog","Zero defects, zero changeovers, and zero inventory","Tujuan TPM: zero defects, zero breakdowns, zero accidents, ditambah desain tempat kerja yang efektif untuk menurunkan biaya O&M.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Zero inventory dan zero waiting: lebih dekat ke tujuan JIT/lean.\n• Zero overtime dan zero backlog: backlog nol justru tidak sehat (Gulati: 4–6 minggu).\n• Zero changeovers: changeover diperpendek (SMED), bukan dihilangkan.",7],
["Which is NOT one of the eight TPM pillars listed by Gulati?","Total quality management","Autonomous maintenance","Office improvement","Design and early equipment management","Delapan pilar TPM menurut Gulati: (1) autonomous maintenance, (2) focused improvement (kaizen), (3) planned maintenance, (4) quality maintenance, (5) training & development, (6) design & early equipment management, (7) office improvement, (8) safety, health & environment.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Autonomous maintenance, office improvement, dan early equipment management semuanya pilar TPM.\n• TQM adalah program kualitas tersendiri. TPM mirip dan memakai banyak alat TQM, tetapi TQM bukan pilarnya.",7],
["The TPM pillar in which operators clean, lubricate, inspect, and make minor adjustments is:","Autonomous maintenance","Planned maintenance","Quality maintenance","Focused improvement","Autonomous maintenance (jishu hozen) adalah pilar kunci TPM. Operator membersihkan, melumasi, memeriksa, mengencangkan, membuat penyetelan kecil, dan melaporkan kelainan pada mesin yang mereka operasikan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Planned maintenance: PM dan PdM yang dijalankan departemen maintenance.\n• Quality maintenance: menjaga kondisi peralatan agar produk bebas cacat.\n• Focused improvement: proyek kaizen untuk menghilangkan kerugian spesifik.",7],
["The TPM pillar also called kobetsu kaizen is:","Focused improvement","Autonomous maintenance","Quality maintenance","Planned maintenance","Kobetsu kaizen = focused improvement: tim lintas fungsi menyerang kerugian spesifik (mis. salah satu six big losses) secara terfokus.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Autonomous maintenance = jishu hozen.\n• Quality maintenance = hinshitsu hozen.\n• Planned maintenance = keikaku hozen.",7],
["Which TPM pillar feeds lessons from existing equipment into the design of new equipment?","Design and early equipment management","Focused improvement (kobetsu kaizen)","Quality maintenance","Planned maintenance","Pilar design & early equipment management memasukkan pengalaman operasi dan perawatan dari peralatan yang ada ke spesifikasi dan desain peralatan baru (maintenance prevention), sehingga mesin baru lebih andal, mudah dirawat, dan cepat mencapai kinerja penuh.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Focused improvement: memperbaiki kerugian di peralatan yang sudah ada.\n• Quality maintenance: kondisi peralatan untuk mutu produk.\n• Planned maintenance: jadwal PM/PdM.",7],
["Gulati describes TPM as:","An organization-wide equipment improvement strategy","A maintenance department improvement strategy","An operator training program for basic maintenance","A housekeeping program to keep equipment clean","Gulati menegaskan TPM adalah strategi perbaikan peralatan untuk seluruh organisasi, bukan strategi perbaikan perawatan. TPM melibatkan semua karyawan dari operator hingga eksekutif.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Strategi departemen maintenance saja: Gulati secara eksplisit menolak pandangan ini.\n• Program pelatihan operator: pelatihan hanya satu pilar.\n• Program kebersihan: Gulati menyebut TPM bukan sekadar membersihkan dan mengecat peralatan.",7],
["TPM has the potential to provide almost seamless integration between:","Production and maintenance","Maintenance and quality","Production and engineering","Maintenance and purchasing","TPM adalah pendekatan tim di mana produksi dan perawatan bekerja bersama agar aset beroperasi aman dengan breakdown minimal. Inilah integrasi yang hampir mulus (seamless) menurut Gulati.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Maintenance–quality dan production–engineering: kerja sama juga terjadi, tetapi inti TPM adalah produksi + perawatan.\n• Maintenance–purchasing: tidak terkait.",7],
["In some world-class TPM organizations, newly hired maintenance employees first:","Work on the production lines under operations","Spend six months in the storeroom","Work alongside the planners for their first months","Complete a full RCM analysis course","Di beberapa organisasi TPM kelas dunia, karyawan maintenance baru dilatih mengoperasikan lini produksi di bawah departemen operasi sebelum pindah ke maintenance. Tujuannya mewariskan pengetahuan operator, membangun kerja sama, dan memecah sekat budaya.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Enam bulan di gudang, ikut planner, atau kursus RCM penuh: bermanfaat, tetapi bukan praktik yang disebut Gulati.",7],
["Which is a benefit of TPM cited by Gulati?","Fewer short stoppages","Fewer maintenance technicians","Lower spare parts inventory","Shorter planning lead times","Manfaat TPM menurut Gulati: tempat kerja lebih aman, karyawan lebih berdaya dan bermoral tinggi, output naik, cacat minimal, breakdown minimal, short stoppage berkurang, waste berkurang, dan biaya O&M turun.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Teknisi lebih sedikit: TPM bukan program pengurangan staf.\n• Inventori spare lebih rendah dan lead time planning lebih pendek: tidak disebut sebagai manfaat TPM.",7],
["The original 5S consists of:","Sort, set in order, shine, standardize, sustain","Sort, set in order, shine, safety, sustain","Sort, straighten, sweep, schedule, sustain","Sort, set in order, sanitize, standardize, safety","5S asli: Sort (seiri), Set in order (seiton), Shine (seiso), Standardize (seiketsu), Sustain (shitsuke).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Ada Safety: itu S keenam (6S), bukan bagian 5S asli.\n• Sweep dan schedule: 'straighten' dan 'sweep' adalah terjemahan alternatif, tetapi 'schedule' bukan bagian 5S.\n• Sanitize dan safety: bukan 5S asli.",7],
["In 6S (5S plus), the sixth S stands for:","Safety","Security","Satisfaction","Spirit","6S (5S plus) menambahkan Safety sebagai S keenam untuk menekankan keselamatan di tempat kerja.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Security, Satisfaction, Spirit: tidak dipakai dalam konsep 6S yang dijelaskan Gulati.",7],
["Which S involves cleaning the equipment and using cleaning as a form of inspection?","Shine (seiso)","Standardize (seiketsu)","Set in order (seiton)","Sustain (shitsuke)","Shine (seiso) adalah membersihkan area dan peralatan. Dalam TPM, 'cleaning is inspecting': saat membersihkan, operator menemukan kebocoran, baut longgar, retak, dan kelainan lain.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Standardize: membakukan praktik 3S pertama.\n• Set in order: menata barang di tempatnya.\n• Sustain: disiplin mempertahankan semuanya.",7],
["Which S involves removing unneeded items from the work area?","Sort (seiri)","Set in order (seiton)","Shine (seiso)","Standardize (seiketsu)","Sort (seiri) adalah memisahkan barang yang diperlukan dari yang tidak diperlukan, lalu menyingkirkan yang tidak perlu (sering memakai 'red tag').\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Set in order: menata barang yang tersisa.\n• Shine: membersihkan.\n• Standardize: membakukan.",7],
["Which S means 'a place for everything and everything in its place'?","Set in order (seiton)","Sort (seiri)","Standardize (seiketsu)","Shine (seiso)","Set in order (seiton): 'a place for everything and everything in its place'. Barang ditata, diberi label atau shadow board, dan diletakkan dekat titik pemakaian agar mudah diambil dan dikembalikan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Sort: menyingkirkan barang yang tidak perlu.\n• Standardize: membakukan metode.\n• Shine: membersihkan.",7],
["Which S is usually the hardest because it relies on discipline and habit?","Sustain (shitsuke)","Standardize (seiketsu)","Set in order (seiton)","Sort (seiri)","Sustain (shitsuke) membutuhkan disiplin dan kebiasaan agar 4S sebelumnya tidak kembali ke kondisi lama. Karena itu Sustain paling sulit; inilah tahap tempat banyak program 5S gagal.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Standardize, Set in order, Sort: bersifat 'proyek' sekali jalan yang relatif mudah dimulai; tantangannya adalah mempertahankannya.",7],
["A visual workplace is one in which:","Anyone can understand the process status and spot abnormalities at a glance","Procedures and drawings are displayed on screens at each workstation","Supervisors can monitor each operator from a central location","Performance data is posted weekly on a notice board","Visual workplace memakai tanda, label, warna, dan marking sehingga siapa pun, bahkan yang tidak mengenal prosesnya, bisa langsung memahami status proses dan mengenali kondisi abnormal.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Prosedur di layar setiap workstation: membantu, tetapi inti visual workplace adalah status normal/abnormal yang terlihat seketika.\n• Supervisor memantau dari pusat: itu pengawasan, bukan manajemen visual.\n• Data kinerja mingguan di papan: terlalu jarang dan tidak menunjukkan kondisi saat ini.",7],
["Color-coded labels on piping, hoses, and valves are an example of:","Visual management","Poka-yoke","Standard work","Kanban","Label berwarna pada pipa, selang, dan valve adalah contoh visual management. Arah aliran, isi, dan status langsung terlihat.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Poka-yoke: perangkat yang mencegah kesalahan secara fisik.\n• Standard work: urutan kerja baku.\n• Kanban: sinyal tarik untuk aliran material.",7],
["The OEE loss 'setup and adjustment' belongs to which factor?","Availability","Performance","Quality","Utilization","Six big losses: availability = breakdown + setup/adjustment; performance = small stops/idling + reduced speed; quality = startup rejects + production rejects. Setup dan adjustment menghentikan produksi, sehingga mengurangi availability.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Performance: kecepatan dan stop kecil.\n• Quality: produk cacat.\n• Utilization: faktor TEEP, bukan OEE.",7],
["Running a machine below its designed speed reduces which OEE factor?","Performance","Availability","Quality","Utilization","Mesin yang berjalan di bawah kecepatan desain (reduced speed) menurunkan faktor performance OEE (ideal cycle time × jumlah ÷ run time).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Availability: mesin tetap berjalan, jadi bukan downtime.\n• Quality: produk bisa tetap baik.\n• Utilization: bukan faktor OEE.",7],
["Small stops and idling are classified as which OEE loss?","Performance","Availability","Quality","Utilization","Small stops (minor stoppages) dan idling biasanya terlalu singkat untuk dicatat sebagai downtime, sehingga muncul sebagai kehilangan kecepatan, yaitu kerugian performance.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Availability: untuk breakdown dan setup yang tercatat.\n• Quality: untuk produk cacat.\n• Utilization: bukan faktor OEE.",7],
["Startup rejects reduce which OEE factor?","Quality","Performance","Availability","Utilization","Startup rejects (reduced yield), yaitu produk cacat saat start-up hingga proses stabil, mengurangi faktor quality.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Performance: kecepatan dan stop kecil.\n• Availability: downtime.\n• Utilization: bukan faktor OEE.",7],
["[Calc] Planned production time is 480 minutes and downtime is 48 minutes. What is availability?","90%","91%","89%","10%","Rumus:\n  Availability (OEE) = Run time ÷ Planned production time\n  Run time = Planned production time − Downtime\n\nDiketahui:\n  Planned time = 480 menit, downtime = 48 menit\n\nLangkah:\n1) Run time = 480 − 48 = 432 menit\n2) 432 ÷ 480 = 0,90\n\nJawaban: 90%.",7],
["[Calc] Ideal cycle time is 1 minute; 400 units were produced in 432 minutes of run time. The performance rate is:","92.6%","83.3%","90.0%","108%","Rumus:\n  Performance = (Ideal cycle time × Total count) ÷ Run time\n\nDiketahui:\n  Ideal cycle time = 1 menit/unit, total count = 400 unit, run time = 432 menit\n\nLangkah:\n1) Waktu ideal = 1 × 400 = 400 menit\n2) 400 ÷ 432 = 0,926\n\nJawaban: 92,6%.\nJebakan: 400 ÷ 480 = 83,3% memakai planned time, padahal downtime sudah dihitung di availability.",7],
["[Calc] Of 400 units produced, 8 were defective. The quality rate is:","98%","97%","92%","99%","Rumus:\n  Quality = Good count ÷ Total count\n  Good count = Total count − Defect count\n\nDiketahui:\n  Total = 400 unit, cacat = 8 unit\n\nLangkah:\n1) Good count = 400 − 8 = 392\n2) 392 ÷ 400 = 0,98\n\nJawaban: 98%.",7],
["Gulati defines Lean as:","A practice of waste identification and elimination","A practice of reducing variation and defects in processes","A system for leveling production volume","A method for continuous incremental improvement","Gulati mendefinisikan Lean sebagai praktik mengidentifikasi dan menghilangkan pemborosan (waste/muda), yaitu aktivitas yang tidak menambah nilai bagi pelanggan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Mengurangi variasi dan cacat: fokus Six Sigma.\n• Meratakan volume produksi: heijunka, salah satu alat lean.\n• Perbaikan bertahap berkelanjutan: kaizen, filosofi yang mendukung lean.",11],
["Muda, mura, and muri mean, respectively:","Waste, unevenness, and overburden","Waste, overburden, and unevenness","Unevenness, waste, and overburden","Overburden, unevenness, and waste","Tiga M lean: Muda = waste (aktivitas tanpa nilai tambah), Mura = unevenness (ketidakrataan atau inkonsistensi), Muri = overburden (beban berlebih pada orang atau mesin).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Ketiga pilihan lain hanya menukar urutan arti mura dan muri atau muda. Hafalkan: Muda-Waste, mUra-Uneven, muRi-beRat.",7],
["Which is NOT one of the classic seven wastes of Lean?","Underutilized talent","Overproduction","Waiting","Overprocessing","Tujuh waste klasik (TIMWOOD): Transportation, Inventory, Motion, Waiting, Overproduction, Overprocessing, Defects. Underutilized talent (skills) adalah waste kedelapan yang ditambahkan belakangan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Overproduction, Waiting, dan Overprocessing semuanya termasuk tujuh waste klasik.",11],
["Which waste is often considered the worst because it creates other wastes?","Overproduction","Waiting","Defects","Motion","Overproduction dianggap waste terburuk karena memicu waste lain: inventori menumpuk, transportasi dan penanganan bertambah, ruang terpakai, dan masalah (cacat) tersembunyi di dalam tumpukan stok.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Waiting, Defects, Motion: tetap waste, tetapi biasanya tidak menjadi sumber waste lain seperti overproduction.",11],
["Kanban is best described as:","A visual signal used to trigger and control material flow","A board used to display and track the daily maintenance schedule","A system for leveling production volume and mix","A visual alarm that indicates a process problem","Kanban ('kartu' atau 'sinyal visual') memicu dan mengendalikan aliran material dalam sistem tarik (pull). Kanban memastikan hanya diproduksi yang diminta pelanggan atau proses hilir.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Papan jadwal maintenance harian: papan visual biasa (meski ada 'kanban board' di dunia IT, ini bukan arti Lean aslinya).\n• Leveling volume dan mix: heijunka.\n• Alarm visual masalah: andon.",7],
["Kaizen means:","Continuous improvement","Workplace","Mistake-proofing","Visual signal","Kaizen berarti perbaikan berkelanjutan: perubahan kecil yang terus-menerus dan melibatkan semua orang.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Workplace = gemba.\n• Mistake-proofing = poka-yoke.\n• Visual signal = kanban (atau andon untuk alarm).",7],
["Gemba refers to:","The place where value is created","The production leveling process","Workplace housekeeping","A daily improvement meeting","Gemba (genba) berarti 'tempat sebenarnya', yaitu lokasi tempat nilai diciptakan, seperti lantai produksi atau lokasi aset.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Leveling produksi: heijunka.\n• Housekeeping: 5S.\n• Rapat perbaikan harian: daily stand-up/tier meeting, bukan arti gemba.",7],
["A poka-yoke is:","A device or method that prevents mistakes or makes them obvious","A visual signal that alerts staff when a machine has stopped running","A standard sequence of work for each operator","A card used to authorize the movement of material","Poka-yoke adalah perangkat atau metode yang mencegah kesalahan (mis. konektor yang hanya bisa dipasang satu arah) atau membuat kesalahan langsung terlihat sebelum menjadi cacat.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Sinyal saat mesin berhenti: andon.\n• Urutan kerja baku: standard work.\n• Kartu otorisasi pergerakan material: kanban.",7],
["Value stream mapping (VSM) is mainly used to:","Show material and information flow and identify waste","Calculate the takt time and cycle time of each process step","Rank causes of downtime by frequency","Measure the capability of a process","Value stream mapping memetakan aliran material dan informasi dari pemasok sampai pelanggan untuk melihat aktivitas yang bernilai tambah dan tidak, lead time, dan lokasi waste. Hasilnya menjadi dasar future-state map.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Menghitung takt dan cycle time: data tersebut dicantumkan di VSM, tetapi bukan tujuan utamanya.\n• Meranking penyebab downtime: Pareto.\n• Mengukur kapabilitas proses: Cp/Cpk.",11],
["Takt time is calculated as:","Available production time ÷ customer demand","Customer demand ÷ available production time","Total cycle time ÷ number of operators","Lead time ÷ work in process","Takt time = waktu produksi tersedia ÷ permintaan pelanggan. Takt time menunjukkan irama produksi yang dibutuhkan agar sesuai permintaan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Permintaan ÷ waktu: menghasilkan laju (unit per menit), kebalikan dari takt.\n• Total cycle time ÷ jumlah operator: dipakai untuk balancing, bukan takt.\n• Lead time ÷ WIP: kebalikan dari throughput dalam Little's Law.",11],
["[Calc] Available time is 450 minutes per shift and customer demand is 900 units per shift. Takt time is:","30 seconds","2 minutes","45 seconds","20 seconds","Rumus:\n  Takt time = Waktu produksi tersedia ÷ Permintaan pelanggan\n\nDiketahui:\n  Waktu tersedia = 450 menit/shift, permintaan = 900 unit/shift\n\nLangkah:\n1) 450 ÷ 900 = 0,5 menit per unit\n2) 0,5 × 60 = 30 detik\n\nJawaban: 30 detik. Jebakan: 900 ÷ 450 = 2 adalah unit per menit, bukan takt time.",11],
["SMED (single minute exchange of die) mainly aims to:","Shorten changeovers by converting internal setup to external setup","Shorten changeovers by adding more operators to the setup crew","Eliminate changeovers by producing larger batches between setups","Reduce setup errors by using poka-yoke devices","SMED (Shigeo Shingo) memperpendek waktu changeover dengan memisahkan aktivitas internal dan eksternal, lalu mengubah sebanyak mungkin aktivitas internal menjadi eksternal (dikerjakan saat mesin masih berjalan) dan menyederhanakan sisanya.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Menambah operator: bisa membantu, tetapi bukan prinsip inti SMED.\n• Batch lebih besar: justru menambah overproduction dan inventori; SMED bertujuan memungkinkan batch kecil.\n• Poka-yoke untuk error setup: alat pelengkap, bukan tujuan utama SMED.",11],
["An internal setup activity is one that:","Can only be done while the machine is stopped","Can be done while the machine is running","Is performed by the operator rather than maintenance","Is performed inside the machine guarding","Aktivitas setup internal hanya dapat dilakukan saat mesin berhenti (mis. mengganti cetakan). Aktivitas eksternal dapat dilakukan saat mesin berjalan (mis. menyiapkan alat dan cetakan berikutnya).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Bisa saat mesin berjalan: itu definisi eksternal.\n• Siapa yang melakukan dan lokasi di dalam guard: tidak menentukan internal atau eksternal.",11],
["An A3 report is:","A structured problem-solving summary on one sheet","A level of maintenance in the TPM framework","A standard format for job plans","A type of process capability study","Laporan A3 adalah pendekatan pemecahan masalah terstruktur (berbasis PDCA) yang diringkas pada satu lembar kertas ukuran A3: latar belakang, kondisi saat ini, analisis akar penyebab, target, tindakan, dan tindak lanjut.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Level perawatan TPM, format job plan, studi kapabilitas: tidak terkait dengan istilah A3.",11],
["Six Sigma is primarily focused on:","Reducing process variation and defects","Eliminating non-value-added activities","Improving equipment availability","Shortening changeover time","Six Sigma berfokus mengurangi variasi proses dan cacat dengan pendekatan statistik dan data (DMAIC), menuju 3,4 DPMO.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Menghilangkan aktivitas tanpa nilai tambah: fokus Lean.\n• Meningkatkan availability peralatan: fokus TPM/RCM.\n• Mempercepat changeover: SMED.\n\nKeduanya sering digabung menjadi Lean Six Sigma.",11],
["The Six Sigma improvement methodology for existing processes is:","DMAIC","DMADV","PDCA","SIPOC","DMAIC (Define, Measure, Analyze, Improve, Control) adalah metodologi Six Sigma untuk memperbaiki proses yang sudah ada.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• DMADV: untuk mendesain proses atau produk baru (Design for Six Sigma).\n• PDCA: siklus perbaikan umum (Deming).\n• SIPOC: alat pemetaan proses yang dipakai di fase Define.",11],
["In DMAIC, control plans and monitoring are put in place to hold the gains during:","Control","Improve","Analyze","Measure","Pada fase Control, control plan, SPC/control chart, prosedur standar, dan pemantauan diterapkan agar perbaikan bertahan dan proses tidak kembali ke kondisi lama.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Improve: solusi dikembangkan dan diuji.\n• Analyze: akar penyebab dicari.\n• Measure: baseline dan sistem pengukuran ditetapkan.",11],
["A Six Sigma process level corresponds to about:","3.4 defects per million opportunities","233 defects per million opportunities","6,210 defects per million opportunities","0.34 defects per million opportunities","Level Six Sigma setara 3,4 cacat per sejuta peluang (DPMO), dengan asumsi pergeseran rata-rata 1,5σ jangka panjang.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• 233 DPMO: setara 5σ.\n• 6.210 DPMO: setara 4σ.\n• 0,34 DPMO: lebih baik dari six sigma, tidak sesuai definisi.",11],
["Process capability index Cp is calculated as:","(USL − LSL) / 6σ","(USL − LSL) / 3σ","(USL − mean) / 3σ","(mean − LSL) / 6σ","Cp = (USL − LSL) ÷ 6σ: perbandingan lebar spesifikasi dengan lebar sebaran proses (±3σ). Cp tidak memperhitungkan letak rata-rata.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Dibagi 3σ: menghasilkan nilai dua kali lipat (salah).\n• (USL − mean) ÷ 3σ: itu Cpu, salah satu sisi Cpk.\n• (mean − LSL) ÷ 6σ: pembaginya salah; sisi bawah Cpk memakai 3σ.",11],
["[Calc] USL = 10.6, LSL = 9.4, σ = 0.1. What is Cp?","2.0","1.0","4.0","1.2","Rumus:\n  Cp = (USL − LSL) ÷ 6σ\n\nDiketahui:\n  USL = 10,6; LSL = 9,4; σ = 0,1\n\nLangkah:\n1) Lebar spesifikasi = 10,6 − 9,4 = 1,2\n2) Lebar proses = 6 × 0,1 = 0,6\n3) Cp = 1,2 ÷ 0,6 = 2,0\n\nJebakan: membagi dengan 3σ menghasilkan 4,0.",11],
["[Calc] USL = 10.6, LSL = 9.4, mean = 10.3, σ = 0.1. What is Cpk?","1.0","2.0","3.0","1.5","Rumus:\n  Cpk = min[(USL − μ) ÷ 3σ ; (μ − LSL) ÷ 3σ]\n\nDiketahui:\n  USL = 10,6; LSL = 9,4; μ = 10,3; σ = 0,1 → 3σ = 0,3\n\nLangkah:\n1) Sisi atas: (10,6 − 10,3) ÷ 0,3 = 0,3 ÷ 0,3 = 1,0\n2) Sisi bawah: (10,3 − 9,4) ÷ 0,3 = 0,9 ÷ 0,3 = 3,0\n3) Ambil yang terkecil: Cpk = 1,0\n\nCatatan: Cp = 2,0 tetapi Cpk = 1,0 karena rata-rata proses bergeser mendekati USL.",11],
["Compared with Cp, the Cpk index additionally accounts for:","How well the process is centered","How large the sample size is","Whether the data is normally distributed","How stable the process is over time","Cpk menambahkan faktor centering: seberapa dekat rata-rata proses ke batas spesifikasi terdekat. Jika proses tepat di tengah, Cpk = Cp; jika bergeser, Cpk < Cp.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Ukuran sampel: memengaruhi keyakinan estimasi, bukan definisi Cpk.\n• Distribusi normal: asumsi keduanya, bukan pembeda.\n• Stabilitas proses: dinilai dengan control chart; Cp dan Cpk sama-sama mengasumsikan proses stabil.",11],
["A Cpk of at least what value is commonly considered capable?","1.33","1.00","0.67","2.50","Cpk ≥ 1,33 umumnya dianggap capable. Artinya ada jarak 4σ dari rata-rata ke batas spesifikasi terdekat. Banyak industri (mis. otomotif) mensyaratkan 1,33 atau 1,67.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• 1,00: proses tepat menyentuh batas pada ±3σ, tanpa margin (sekitar 0,27% di luar spesifikasi).\n• 0,67: tidak capable.\n• 2,50: sangat baik, tetapi bukan ambang umum.",11],
["Variation that is inherent and random in a stable process is called:","Common cause variation","Special cause variation","Assignable cause variation","Systematic variation","Common cause variation adalah variasi alami dan acak yang melekat pada sistem yang stabil. Untuk menguranginya, sistemnya harus diubah.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Special cause dan assignable cause: dua istilah untuk hal yang sama, yaitu penyebab spesifik yang dapat diidentifikasi (mis. tool aus, bahan baku berbeda).\n• Systematic variation: bukan istilah standar SPC untuk variasi acak.",11],
["A point outside the control limits on a control chart usually indicates:","A special cause that should be investigated","A common cause inherent in the process","That the specification limits must be revised","That the process is not capable","Titik di luar batas kendali (±3σ) menandakan special (assignable) cause, yaitu sesuatu yang berubah pada proses, sehingga harus diselidiki dan dihilangkan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Common cause: variasi acak biasanya tetap di dalam batas.\n• Revisi batas spesifikasi: batas spesifikasi berasal dari pelanggan, bukan dari control chart.\n• Proses tidak capable: kapabilitas dinilai terhadap spesifikasi (Cp/Cpk), bukan dari titik di luar control limit.",11],
["Control limits on a control chart are calculated from:","Process data","Customer specifications","Engineering tolerances","Historical targets","Control limit dihitung dari data proses itu sendiri (rata-rata ± 3σ proses). Control limit menunjukkan 'suara proses'.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Spesifikasi pelanggan dan toleransi engineering: itu batas spesifikasi ('suara pelanggan'), yang tidak digambar sebagai control limit.\n• Target historis: bukan dasar statistik control chart.",11],
["Which chart monitors the proportion of defective units?","p-chart","c-chart","u-chart","X-bar and R chart","p-chart memantau proporsi (fraksi) unit cacat; ukuran sampel boleh bervariasi.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• c-chart: jumlah cacat per sampel dengan ukuran tetap.\n• u-chart: jumlah cacat per unit dengan ukuran sampel bervariasi.\n• X-bar dan R: data variabel (pengukuran), bukan atribut.",11],
["Which chart monitors the count of defects in samples of constant size?","c-chart","p-chart","np-chart","X-bar and S chart","c-chart memantau jumlah cacat (count of defects) dalam sampel atau area pemeriksaan berukuran tetap. Satu unit bisa memiliki lebih dari satu cacat.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• p-chart: proporsi unit cacat.\n• np-chart: jumlah unit cacat (bukan jumlah cacat) dengan sampel tetap.\n• X-bar dan S: data variabel.",11],
["For a normal distribution, about what percentage of values fall within ±3σ of the mean?","99.73%","95.45%","99.99%","68.27%","Pada distribusi normal: ±1σ ≈ 68,27%, ±2σ ≈ 95,45%, ±3σ ≈ 99,73%. Inilah dasar batas kendali ±3σ.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• 95,45% = ±2σ; 68,27% = ±1σ; 99,99% mendekati ±4σ.",11],
["A Pareto chart helps to:","Identify the vital few causes behind most of a problem","Show how a process varies over time","Show the relationship between two variables","Show possible causes of a problem grouped by category","Pareto chart (prinsip 80/20) mengurutkan penyebab dari frekuensi atau dampak terbesar, sehingga 'vital few' yang menyumbang sebagian besar masalah terlihat jelas.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Variasi dari waktu ke waktu: run chart atau control chart.\n• Hubungan dua variabel: scatter diagram.\n• Kemungkinan penyebab per kategori: diagram fishbone (Ishikawa).",11],
["A maintenance engineer has a list of pump failure modes and their frequencies. Which tool best helps prioritize them?","Pareto chart","Fishbone diagram","Scatter diagram","Control chart","Dengan daftar failure mode beserta frekuensinya, Pareto chart menunjukkan failure mode mana yang paling sering terjadi sehingga perbaikan diprioritaskan pada yang paling berdampak. Ini juga jawaban Gulati di tes Bab 1.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Fishbone: mencari kemungkinan penyebab satu masalah, bukan meranking.\n• Scatter: korelasi dua variabel.\n• Control chart: stabilitas proses dari waktu ke waktu.",11],
["The 80/20 principle is named after:","Vilfredo Pareto","Joseph Juran","Walter Shewhart","Kaoru Ishikawa","Prinsip 80/20 dinamai dari Vilfredo Pareto, ekonom Italia yang mengamati 80% tanah dimiliki 20% penduduk. Joseph Juran kemudian mempopulerkannya di bidang kualitas sebagai 'vital few, trivial many'.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Juran: mempopulerkan, tetapi bukan asal nama.\n• Shewhart: control chart.\n• Ishikawa: fishbone.",11],
["The cause-and-effect (fishbone) diagram was developed by:","Kaoru Ishikawa","Joseph Juran","Genichi Taguchi","W. Edwards Deming","Diagram cause-and-effect (fishbone) dikembangkan oleh Kaoru Ishikawa, sehingga disebut juga diagram Ishikawa.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Juran: trilogi kualitas, Pareto untuk kualitas.\n• Taguchi: robust design dan loss function.\n• Deming: PDCA dan 14 poin manajemen.",11],
["Typical categories of a manufacturing fishbone diagram (6M) include:","Man, machine, method, material, measurement, mother nature","Man, machine, method, money, management, maintenance","Material, method, machine, market, motivation, measurement","Man, money, method, material, maintenance, mother nature","Kategori 6M fishbone manufaktur: Man (manusia), Machine, Method, Material, Measurement, Mother nature (lingkungan).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Money, management, maintenance, market, motivation: kadang muncul di variasi lain (mis. 8M atau 4P untuk layanan), tetapi bukan 6M standar manufaktur.",11],
["A scatter diagram is used to:","Show the relationship between two variables","Show the frequency distribution of data","Show the sequence of process steps","Show variation over time against limits","Scatter diagram memplot pasangan data dua variabel untuk melihat ada tidaknya hubungan atau korelasi (positif, negatif, tidak ada). Korelasi belum tentu sebab-akibat.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Distribusi frekuensi: histogram.\n• Urutan langkah proses: flowchart.\n• Variasi terhadap batas dari waktu ke waktu: control chart.",11],
["A histogram shows:","The frequency distribution of data","The correlation between two variables","The trend of data over time","The ranking of causes by impact","Histogram menampilkan distribusi frekuensi data: bentuk, pusat, dan sebarannya (mis. apakah normal atau miring).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Korelasi dua variabel: scatter diagram.\n• Tren dari waktu ke waktu: run chart.\n• Ranking penyebab: Pareto.",11],
["The 5 whys technique is used to:","Drill down to a root cause by repeatedly asking why","Identify five categories of possible causes","Rank failure modes by risk priority number","Verify a solution with five test runs","5 whys menelusuri akar penyebab dengan bertanya 'mengapa?' berulang kali (sekitar lima kali, tidak harus tepat lima) sampai menemukan penyebab yang dapat dikoreksi.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Lima kategori penyebab: mirip fishbone.\n• Meranking dengan RPN: FMEA.\n• Lima kali uji coba: tidak terkait.",11],
["In an FMEA, the RPN is calculated as:","Severity × occurrence × detection","Severity + occurrence + detection","Severity × occurrence","Occurrence × detection ÷ severity","RPN (risk priority number) = Severity × Occurrence × Detection. Masing-masing biasanya berskala 1–10, sehingga RPN berkisar 1–1000.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Dijumlah: Gulati menegaskan perkalian, bukan penjumlahan.\n• S × O saja: itu criticality sederhana (tanpa detection).\n• O × D ÷ S: bukan rumus FMEA.",11],
["A process FMEA (PFMEA) focuses on:","Failure modes of manufacturing or assembly process steps","Failure modes of the product's design features and its components","Failure modes of equipment in operation","Hazards to workers performing each process step","Process FMEA (PFMEA) menganalisis potensi failure mode pada langkah proses manufaktur atau perakitan (mis. torsi kurang, part terbalik) beserta efek dan kontrolnya.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Fitur desain produk: itu Design FMEA (DFMEA).\n• Peralatan yang beroperasi: FMEA atau FMECA peralatan (dalam RCM).\n• Bahaya bagi pekerja: Job Safety Analysis (JSA).",11],
["The AIAG & VDA FMEA Handbook replaced RPN-based prioritization with:","Action priority (AP)","Criticality number (Cm)","Severity-based ranking","Risk matrix scoring","Handbook FMEA AIAG & VDA (2019) mengganti prioritas berbasis RPN dengan Action Priority (AP: High/Medium/Low), yang memberi bobot lebih besar pada severity.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Criticality number (Cm): dipakai di FMECA (MIL-STD-1629).\n• Ranking berdasarkan severity saja: AP mempertimbangkan S, O, dan D.\n• Skoring matriks risiko: bukan metode AIAG-VDA.",11],
["SIPOC stands for:","Suppliers, inputs, process, outputs, customers","Standards, inputs, process, outputs, controls","Suppliers, inspection, process, outputs, controls","Scope, inputs, process, outcomes, customers","SIPOC = Suppliers, Inputs, Process, Outputs, Customers. SIPOC adalah peta proses tingkat tinggi yang dipakai di fase Define untuk menetapkan batas proyek.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Standards, controls, inspection, scope, outcomes: kata-kata yang terdengar mirip, tetapi bukan isi SIPOC.",11],
["Critical-to-quality (CTQ) characteristics are derived from:","The voice of the customer","The process control plan","The process FMEA","The supplier specifications","Karakteristik CTQ (critical-to-quality) diturunkan dari voice of the customer (VOC): kebutuhan pelanggan diterjemahkan menjadi karakteristik terukur dengan spesifikasi.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Control plan dan PFMEA: dokumen yang memakai CTQ sebagai masukan, bukan sumbernya.\n• Spesifikasi pemasok: berkaitan dengan input, bukan kebutuhan pelanggan.",11],
["Design of experiments (DOE) is useful because it:","Tests the effects of several factors and their interactions together","Tests one factor at a time while holding other factors constant","Monitors the process over time against control limits","Ranks the causes of defects by their frequency","Design of experiments (DOE) menguji beberapa faktor secara bersamaan secara terstruktur, sehingga efek tiap faktor dan interaksinya dapat diketahui dengan jumlah percobaan yang efisien.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Satu faktor pada satu waktu (OFAT): pendekatan tradisional yang tidak bisa mendeteksi interaksi.\n• Memantau proses terhadap control limit: SPC.\n• Meranking penyebab cacat: Pareto.",11],
["Defect elimination is best described as:","Systematically finding and removing the sources of defects before they cause losses","Inspecting products more frequently so defects are caught before they reach the customer","Replacing components more often to prevent defects from developing","Recording defects in the CMMS for future analysis","Defect elimination adalah upaya sistematis menemukan dan menghilangkan sumber cacat (desain, instalasi, operasi, perawatan) sebelum menimbulkan kegagalan atau kerugian. Ini pendekatan proaktif.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Inspeksi lebih sering: hanya menyaring cacat, tidak menghilangkan sumbernya.\n• Mengganti komponen lebih sering: bisa menambah maintenance-induced defects.\n• Mencatat di CMMS: dokumentasi tanpa tindakan.",11],
["[Calc] Little's Law: throughput is 20 units per hour and lead time is 3 hours. Average work in process is:","60 units","6.7 units","23 units","15 units","Rumus (Little's Law):\n  WIP = Throughput × Lead time\n\nDiketahui:\n  Throughput = 20 unit/jam, lead time = 3 jam\n\nLangkah:\n1) 20 × 3 = 60\n\nJawaban: 60 unit. Jebakan: 20 ÷ 3 = 6,7 membalik rumus.",11],
["[Calc] Three process steps have yields of 95%, 98%, and 90%. The rolled throughput yield is about:","83.8%","94.3%","90.0%","86.5%","Rumus:\n  Rolled throughput yield (RTY) = Y1 × Y2 × Y3 × …\n\nDiketahui:\n  Y1 = 0,95; Y2 = 0,98; Y3 = 0,90\n\nLangkah:\n1) 0,95 × 0,98 = 0,931\n2) 0,931 × 0,90 = 0,8379\n\nJawaban: ≈ 83,8%.\nJebakan: rata-rata (0,95 + 0,98 + 0,90) ÷ 3 = 94,3% bukan RTY.",11],
["According to the theory of constraints, an hour lost at the bottleneck is:","An hour lost for the entire system","Recovered by faster non-bottleneck steps","Less costly than an hour lost upstream","Absorbed by the buffer after the bottleneck","Dalam theory of constraints, throughput sistem ditentukan oleh bottleneck. Satu jam yang hilang di bottleneck adalah satu jam yang hilang bagi seluruh sistem dan tidak dapat dipulihkan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Dipulihkan oleh langkah non-bottleneck yang lebih cepat: kapasitas lebih mereka tidak dapat menambah output bottleneck.\n• Lebih murah dari jam yang hilang di hulu: justru sebaliknya; jam yang hilang di non-bottleneck sering tidak berdampak.\n• Diserap buffer setelah bottleneck: buffer ditempatkan sebelum bottleneck untuk melindunginya; output yang hilang tetap hilang.",11],
["The first of the theory of constraints five focusing steps is:","Identify the constraint","Exploit the constraint","Elevate the constraint","Subordinate to the constraint","Lima langkah fokus TOC (Goldratt): (1) Identify the constraint, (2) Exploit, (3) Subordinate everything else, (4) Elevate, (5) ulangi dan hindari inersia.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Exploit, Subordinate, Elevate: langkah 2–4; semuanya membutuhkan constraint yang sudah teridentifikasi.",11],
["From a process reliability perspective, maintenance priority should usually go first to:","Bottleneck and critical assets","Assets with the most work requests","Assets with the highest RAV","Assets nearest the end of their life","Dari sudut pandang keandalan proses, prioritas perawatan diberikan pertama kepada aset bottleneck dan aset kritikal (keselamatan, produksi), karena kegagalannya langsung mengurangi output sistem atau menimbulkan risiko besar.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Aset dengan work request terbanyak: belum tentu kritikal.\n• RAV tertinggi: nilai aset bukan ukuran kritikalitas.\n• Mendekati akhir umur: bisa relevan, tetapi bukan dasar prioritas utama.",4],
["Heijunka refers to:","Leveling production volume and mix","Stopping the line when a defect occurs","Pulling material based on consumption","Continuous incremental improvement","Heijunka adalah meratakan (leveling) volume dan mix produksi dalam suatu periode, sehingga beban kerja dan permintaan material stabil (mengurangi mura).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Menghentikan lini saat cacat: jidoka.\n• Menarik material sesuai konsumsi: pull/kanban.\n• Perbaikan berkelanjutan: kaizen.",11],
["Jidoka means:","Automation with a human touch that stops on abnormalities","Producing what is needed, when it is needed, in the amount needed","Continuous incremental improvement involving employees","Leveling production to smooth demand","Jidoka berarti 'automation with a human touch': mesin atau proses berhenti otomatis saat terjadi kelainan, sehingga cacat tidak diteruskan dan masalah segera ditangani. Jidoka adalah salah satu pilar TPS.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Memproduksi yang dibutuhkan, saat dibutuhkan, sejumlah yang dibutuhkan: Just-in-Time, pilar TPS lainnya.\n• Perbaikan bertahap: kaizen.\n• Meratakan produksi: heijunka.",11],
["An andon is:","A signal that alerts people to a problem in the process","A card that authorizes production or material movement","A board showing the planned production sequence","A device that prevents an operator from making errors","Andon adalah sinyal visual atau suara (lampu, papan) yang memberi tahu bahwa ada masalah di proses, sering dipicu operator dengan menarik tali atau menekan tombol.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Kartu otorisasi produksi: kanban.\n• Papan urutan produksi: heijunka box atau production board.\n• Perangkat pencegah kesalahan: poka-yoke.",11],
["Management of change (MOC) is required for:","Process or equipment changes that are not replacements in kind, including temporary ones","Permanent process changes, since temporary changes are covered by work permits","Work orders that involve replacing parts on hazardous equipment","Organizational changes, such as new reporting structures","MOC wajib untuk setiap perubahan proses, teknologi, peralatan, atau prosedur yang bukan replacement in kind, termasuk perubahan sementara. Perubahan sementara justru sering menjadi sumber insiden.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Hanya permanen: perubahan sementara juga memerlukan MOC.\n• Setiap penggantian part pada peralatan berbahaya: penggantian 'in kind' tidak memerlukan MOC.\n• Perubahan organisasi: ada MOC organisasi, tetapi definisi utama MOC dalam PSM adalah perubahan proses dan peralatan.",13],
["A replacement that satisfies the original design specification is called:","Replacement in kind","Like-for-better replacement","Minor modification","Temporary change","Replacement in kind adalah penggantian yang memenuhi spesifikasi desain aslinya (bisa sama persis atau setara). Penggantian ini tidak memerlukan MOC.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Like-for-better: mengubah spesifikasi, sehingga memerlukan MOC.\n• Minor modification: tetap modifikasi, sehingga MOC berlaku.\n• Temporary change: perubahan sementara, juga memerlukan MOC.",13],
["The OSHA standard that requires management of change and process hazard analysis for highly hazardous chemicals is:","Process safety management (29 CFR 1910.119)","Hazardous energy control (29 CFR 1910.147)","Permit-required confined spaces (29 CFR 1910.146)","Hazard communication (29 CFR 1910.1200)","OSHA 29 CFR 1910.119, Process Safety Management of Highly Hazardous Chemicals, mensyaratkan 14 elemen, antara lain PHA, MOC, mechanical integrity, PSSR, dan operating procedures.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• 1910.147: LOTO.\n• 1910.146: confined space.\n• 1910.1200: hazard communication (label, SDS).",13],
["HAZOP studies use guide words such as:","No, more, less, and reverse","What if, why, and how","Severity, occurrence, and detection","Who, what, where, and when","HAZOP memakai guide word (No/None, More, Less, As well as, Part of, Reverse, Other than) yang dikombinasikan dengan parameter proses (flow, pressure, temperature) untuk menemukan deviasi dari maksud desain.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• What if: metode PHA lain (What-If analysis).\n• Severity, occurrence, detection: FMEA.\n• Who, what, where, when: pertanyaan investigasi umum.",13],
["A pre-startup safety review (PSSR) is performed:","Before hazardous materials are introduced into new or modified equipment","After a process incident and before the process is restarted by operations","At the start of each shift by the operating crew","Before maintenance work on running equipment","PSSR dilakukan sebelum bahan berbahaya dimasukkan ke fasilitas baru atau yang dimodifikasi, untuk memastikan konstruksi sesuai desain, prosedur siap, PHA/MOC selesai, dan pelatihan sudah dilakukan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Setelah insiden: investigasi insiden; restart bisa memerlukan PSSR jika ada modifikasi.\n• Awal setiap shift: serah terima shift.\n• Sebelum perawatan pada peralatan berjalan: izin kerja dan JSA.",13],
["Bypassing a safety interlock to keep production running should:","Require formal authorization and controls, such as MOC","Be decided by the shift supervisor on duty and noted in the log","Be recorded in the shift log","Be allowed for no more than one shift","Bypass interlock keselamatan menghilangkan satu lapisan proteksi. Karena itu bypass harus memiliki otorisasi formal, penilaian risiko, kontrol pengganti, dan batas waktu, biasanya melalui MOC atau prosedur bypass yang disetujui.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Diputuskan supervisor dan dicatat di log: tidak cukup tanpa penilaian risiko formal.\n• Dicatat di log saja: dokumentasi tanpa kontrol.\n• Maksimal satu shift: batas waktu tanpa otorisasi formal tetap berbahaya.",13],
["Arc flash risk is best reduced by:","Working de-energized whenever possible and using proper PPE","Performing infrared scans with the panel doors open on energized gear","Increasing the protective device clearing time","Using non-contact voltage testers before opening panels","Cara terbaik mengurangi risiko arc flash adalah bekerja dalam kondisi de-energized (LOTO) bila memungkinkan, ditambah analisis arc flash, perawatan peralatan listrik, dan APD sesuai NFPA 70E saat pekerjaan energized tidak terhindarkan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Scan IR dengan pintu panel terbuka: menambah paparan; IR window adalah solusinya.\n• Memperpanjang waktu clearing: menambah energi insiden (semakin lama arcing, semakin besar energinya).\n• Voltage tester non-kontak: alat verifikasi, bukan pengendalian utama arc flash.",13],
["Operating equipment outside its design operating window usually:","Accelerates degradation and increases failure rates","Has little effect if PM is performed on time","Mainly affects product quality rather than reliability","Is acceptable if production demand requires it","Mengoperasikan peralatan di luar jendela desain (tekanan, suhu, kecepatan, beban berlebih) mempercepat degradasi mekanisme kegagalan dan menaikkan laju kegagalan, terlepas dari PM.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Efeknya kecil jika PM tepat waktu: PM tidak dapat mengimbangi stres berlebih.\n• Terutama berdampak pada mutu: keandalan juga terdampak langsung.\n• Boleh demi permintaan produksi: risiko kegagalan dan keselamatan meningkat.",7],
["A centrifugal pump operated far from its best efficiency point (BEP) is likely to show:","Higher vibration and shorter seal and bearing life","Lower vibration but higher energy consumption and motor load","Higher efficiency at reduced flow","Longer bearing life due to lower load","Pompa sentrifugal yang beroperasi jauh dari BEP (flow terlalu rendah atau tinggi) mengalami beban radial yang lebih besar, resirkulasi, dan potensi kavitasi, sehingga getaran naik dan umur seal serta bearing memendek.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Getaran lebih rendah: justru meningkat.\n• Efisiensi lebih tinggi pada flow rendah: efisiensi tertinggi ada di BEP.\n• Umur bearing lebih panjang: beban radial justru naik.",8],
["Pump cavitation occurs when:","NPSH available is less than NPSH required","NPSH available is greater than NPSH required","Discharge pressure exceeds design pressure","The pump runs at its best efficiency point","Kavitasi terjadi saat NPSH available (tersedia di sistem) lebih kecil dari NPSH required (dibutuhkan pompa). Tekanan di sisi isap turun di bawah tekanan uap, gelembung uap terbentuk lalu pecah dan merusak impeller.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• NPSHa > NPSHr: kondisi aman.\n• Tekanan discharge berlebih: masalah lain (beban, keselamatan).\n• Operasi di BEP: kondisi optimal.",8],
["Startup and shutdown are considered high-risk periods because:","Conditions change rapidly and non-routine tasks are performed","Operators are usually less experienced at these times","Safety systems are normally bypassed during these periods","Maintenance work is not permitted during these periods","Startup dan shutdown berisiko tinggi karena kondisi proses berubah cepat (transien), banyak tugas non-rutin dan manual, alarm sering aktif, dan prosedurnya jarang dilakukan. Sebagian besar insiden proses terjadi pada periode ini.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Operator kurang berpengalaman: tidak selalu; inti masalahnya kondisi transien.\n• Sistem keselamatan normalnya di-bypass: tidak seharusnya; bypass memerlukan otorisasi.\n• Perawatan tidak diizinkan: tidak menjelaskan mengapa berisiko.",13],
["Standard operating procedures (SOPs) mainly improve process reliability by:","Reducing operator-induced variation","Reducing the need for operator training","Increasing equipment design capacity","Reducing the frequency of PM tasks","SOP memastikan operasi dilakukan dengan cara yang sama setiap kali, sehingga variasi akibat operator berkurang dan proses lebih stabil serta andal.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Mengurangi kebutuhan pelatihan: SOP justru menjadi bahan pelatihan.\n• Menambah kapasitas desain: kapasitas ditentukan desain.\n• Mengurangi frekuensi PM: tidak terkait langsung.",7],
["A Gemba walk is conducted by leaders mainly to:","Observe actual work and understand problems where value is created","Audit compliance with safety rules and issue corrective actions to the area","Review KPI dashboards with area supervisors","Inspect equipment condition before a shutdown","Gemba walk dilakukan pemimpin untuk 'pergi dan melihat' pekerjaan nyata di tempat nilai diciptakan, bertanya, mendengarkan, dan memahami masalah serta hambatan. Tujuannya belajar, bukan mencari kesalahan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Audit keselamatan dan tindakan korektif: itu inspeksi keselamatan; gemba walk bukan audit menghakimi.\n• Meninjau dashboard KPI: bisa dilakukan di ruang rapat; gemba mengutamakan observasi langsung.\n• Inspeksi peralatan sebelum shutdown: tugas teknis.",7],
["Rising differential pressure across a process filter is an indicator of:","Fouling or plugging","Pump cavitation","Reduced fluid viscosity","Seal leakage","Kenaikan ΔP (beda tekanan) di filter menunjukkan filter mulai kotor atau tersumbat (fouling/plugging). Ini indikator kondisi yang sering dipakai untuk menentukan kapan filter diganti (CBM).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Kavitasi pompa: ditandai suara, getaran, dan turunnya tekanan discharge.\n• Viskositas fluida turun: justru menurunkan ΔP.\n• Kebocoran seal: tidak menaikkan ΔP filter.",8],
["Which is a process performance measure Gulati lists under operator-driven reliability?","Output as a percentage of designed or demonstrated capacity","Number of work requests written by maintenance technicians","Percentage of PMs performed by maintenance","Inventory value as a percentage of RAV","Dalam daftar ukuran kinerja ODR (Bab 7), Gulati mencantumkan output sebagai persentase kapasitas desain atau demonstrated capacity, bersama ukuran downtime, 5S, OEE, dan TEEP.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Work request oleh teknisi maintenance: bukan ukuran ODR.\n• % PM oleh maintenance: ukuran ODR justru melihat keterlibatan operator.\n• Nilai inventori % RAV: metrik gudang.",7],
["Under ODR, when corrective maintenance is needed, operators should also be involved in:","Root cause analysis of the failure","Ordering the spare parts","Closing out the work order","Estimating repair labor hours and parts","Dalam ODR, saat perbaikan korektif diperlukan, operator dilibatkan dalam root cause analysis karena mereka mengetahui kondisi operasi sebelum dan saat kegagalan. Hal ini membantu menemukan dan menghilangkan penyebab secara permanen.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Memesan spare part, menutup work order, mengestimasi jam: tugas maintenance, planner, atau teknisi, bukan peran ODR yang ditekankan Gulati.",7],
["OEM maintenance recommendations often lead to too many PM tasks because OEMs:","Lack knowledge of the actual operating context and operator skills","Base their recommendations on RCM analysis of each site","Assume equipment runs fewer hours than it actually does","Are required by regulation to recommend conservative tasks","Rekomendasi OEM sering dibuat tanpa memahami proses, lingkungan operasi aktual, dan keterampilan operator. Akibatnya OEM cenderung meminta lebih banyak tugas dan inspeksi dari yang benar-benar diperlukan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Berbasis RCM per site: justru tidak; RCM spesifik konteks dilakukan pemilik aset.\n• Mengasumsikan jam operasi lebih rendah: bukan alasan yang dikutip Gulati.\n• Diwajibkan regulasi: umumnya tidak.",7],
["Statistical process control charts were originally developed by:","Walter Shewhart","W. Edwards Deming","Joseph Juran","Genichi Taguchi","Control chart dikembangkan Walter Shewhart di Bell Labs pada 1920-an. Deming kemudian mempopulerkannya bersama siklus PDCA (yang juga disebut siklus Shewhart).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Deming: mempopulerkan SPC, tetapi bukan penemunya.\n• Juran: trilogi kualitas.\n• Taguchi: robust design.",11],
["A run of seven or more consecutive points on one side of a control chart's centerline suggests:","A shift in the process even though all points are within limits","Normal variation, because the points remain inside the control limits","That the control limits were calculated incorrectly","That the process capability has improved","Aturan run (Western Electric/Nelson): tujuh atau lebih titik berturut-turut di satu sisi garis tengah menunjukkan pola non-acak, yaitu pergeseran rata-rata proses, walaupun semua titik masih di dalam batas kendali.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Variasi normal karena masih di dalam batas: pola juga menandakan special cause, bukan hanya titik di luar batas.\n• Batas salah hitung: tidak ditunjukkan oleh pola run.\n• Kapabilitas membaik: pergeseran bisa ke arah mana saja dan harus diselidiki.",11],
["The first step of autonomous maintenance in TPM is usually:","Initial cleaning and inspection of the equipment","Training operators in basic lubrication tasks","Developing standards for cleaning and lubrication","Eliminating sources of contamination","Langkah pertama autonomous maintenance adalah pembersihan awal dan inspeksi (initial cleaning). Operator membersihkan mesin secara menyeluruh untuk menemukan kelainan: kebocoran, kotoran, baut longgar, keausan. Prinsipnya 'cleaning is inspecting'.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Eliminasi sumber kontaminasi: langkah ke-2, setelah sumbernya ditemukan saat pembersihan.\n• Standar pembersihan dan pelumasan: langkah ke-3.\n• Pelatihan pelumasan: bagian dari langkah inspeksi umum berikutnya.",7],
["[Calc] Planned time is 480 minutes, downtime 60 minutes, ideal cycle time 0.5 minute, total count 760, and good count 741. The OEE is about:","77.2%","79.2%","85.3%","74.1%","Rumus:\n  A = Run time ÷ Planned time\n  P = (Ideal cycle time × Total count) ÷ Run time\n  Q = Good count ÷ Total count\n  OEE = A × P × Q\n\nLangkah:\n1) Run time = 480 − 60 = 420 menit → A = 420 ÷ 480 = 0,875\n2) P = (0,5 × 760) ÷ 420 = 380 ÷ 420 = 0,905\n3) Q = 741 ÷ 760 = 0,975\n4) OEE = 0,875 × 0,905 × 0,975 = 0,772\n\nCara cepat: OEE = (Good count × Ideal cycle time) ÷ Planned time = (741 × 0,5) ÷ 480 = 370,5 ÷ 480 = 77,2%.\nJebakan: 79,2% = A × P saja.",7],
["[Calc] An asset has an OEE of 75% and a utilization of 80%. Its TEEP is:","60%","75%","94%","55%","Rumus:\n  TEEP = Utilization × OEE\n\nDiketahui:\n  OEE = 75% = 0,75; Utilization = 80% = 0,80\n\nLangkah:\n1) 0,80 × 0,75 = 0,60\n\nJawaban: 60%. TEEP selalu ≤ OEE karena memakai basis 24 jam × 365 hari.",7],
["[Calc] An inspection found 50 defects in 2,000 units, each with 5 defect opportunities. The DPMO is:","5,000","25,000","2,500","10,000","Rumus:\n  DPMO = Jumlah cacat ÷ (Jumlah unit × Peluang cacat per unit) × 1.000.000\n\nDiketahui:\n  Cacat = 50, unit = 2.000, peluang = 5 per unit\n\nLangkah:\n1) Total peluang = 2.000 × 5 = 10.000\n2) 50 ÷ 10.000 = 0,005\n3) 0,005 × 1.000.000 = 5.000\n\nJawaban: 5.000 DPMO.\nJebakan: 50 ÷ 2.000 × 1.000.000 = 25.000 lupa faktor peluang (itu DPPM).",11],
["[Calc] A shift is 8 hours with two 15-minute breaks and a 30-minute lunch. Customer demand is 700 units per shift. Takt time is:","36 seconds","41 seconds","30 seconds","45 seconds","Rumus:\n  Takt time = Waktu produksi tersedia ÷ Permintaan\n  Waktu tersedia = Waktu shift − Istirahat terencana\n\nDiketahui:\n  Shift 8 jam = 480 menit; istirahat 15 + 15 + 30 = 60 menit; permintaan 700 unit\n\nLangkah:\n1) Waktu tersedia = 480 − 60 = 420 menit\n2) 420 ÷ 700 = 0,6 menit per unit\n3) 0,6 × 60 = 36 detik\n\nJebakan: 480 ÷ 700 = 0,686 menit ≈ 41 detik lupa mengurangi istirahat.",11],
["[Calc] USL = 50, LSL = 40, process mean = 44, σ = 1.5. The Cpk is about:","0.89","1.11","1.33","2.00","Rumus:\n  Cp = (USL − LSL) ÷ 6σ\n  Cpk = min[(USL − μ) ÷ 3σ ; (μ − LSL) ÷ 3σ]\n\nDiketahui:\n  USL = 50; LSL = 40; μ = 44; σ = 1,5 → 3σ = 4,5; 6σ = 9\n\nLangkah:\n1) Sisi atas: (50 − 44) ÷ 4,5 = 6 ÷ 4,5 = 1,33\n2) Sisi bawah: (44 − 40) ÷ 4,5 = 4 ÷ 4,5 = 0,89\n3) Cpk = nilai terkecil = 0,89\n\nPembanding: Cp = 10 ÷ 9 = 1,11. Cpk < Cp karena rata-rata lebih dekat ke LSL.",11],
["The elements of standard work are:","Takt time, work sequence, and standard work-in-process","Cycle time, operator count, and in-process quality checks","Work instructions, tools, and safety rules","Takt time, batch size, and changeover time","Standard work (Lean) terdiri dari tiga elemen: takt time, urutan kerja (work sequence), dan standard work-in-process (persediaan minimum dalam proses).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Cycle time, jumlah operator, cek mutu: terkait, tetapi bukan tiga elemen baku.\n• Instruksi kerja, alat, aturan keselamatan: isi SOP umum.\n• Batch size dan changeover: parameter produksi lain.",11],
["A spaghetti diagram is used mainly to show:","The movement of people or material through a work area","The relationship between causes and effects","The flow of information and approvals between departments","The sequence of tasks on the critical path","Spaghetti diagram menggambar jalur perpindahan orang atau material di area kerja. Garis yang kusut menyerupai spageti dan menunjukkan pemborosan gerakan dan transportasi.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Sebab-akibat: fishbone.\n• Aliran informasi dan persetujuan: VSM atau swimlane chart.\n• Urutan tugas jalur kritis: network diagram atau Gantt.",11],
["A kaizen event (kaizen blitz) is:","A focused team improvement effort lasting a few days","A year-long Six Sigma project led by a black belt","A daily meeting to review production problems","An annual award for the best improvement idea","Kaizen event (kaizen blitz) adalah upaya perbaikan intensif oleh tim lintas fungsi, biasanya 3–5 hari, pada satu area atau masalah, dengan implementasi langsung.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Proyek Six Sigma setahun: durasi dan pendekatannya berbeda.\n• Rapat harian: daily stand-up.\n• Penghargaan tahunan: program pengakuan.",11],
["Moving parts back and forth between distant workstations is which Lean waste?","Transportation","Motion","Waiting","Inventory","Memindahkan part bolak-balik antar workstation yang berjauhan adalah waste transportation, yaitu perpindahan material yang tidak menambah nilai.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Motion: gerakan orang (berjalan, meraih, membungkuk).\n• Waiting: menunggu.\n• Inventory: stok berlebih.\n\nIngat: material bergerak = transportation; orang bergerak = motion.",11],
["An operator walking repeatedly to fetch tools from a distant cabinet is which Lean waste?","Motion","Transportation","Overprocessing","Waiting","Operator yang berjalan berulang kali mengambil alat dari lemari jauh adalah waste motion, yaitu gerakan orang yang tidak menambah nilai. Solusinya set in order (5S) dan point-of-use storage.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Transportation: perpindahan material atau produk.\n• Overprocessing: mengerjakan lebih dari yang dibutuhkan pelanggan.\n• Waiting: diam menunggu.",11],
["A pull system means that:","Production is triggered by actual downstream consumption","Production follows a forecast-driven master schedule each week","Material is pushed to the next step when ready","Inventory is built up ahead of seasonal demand","Dalam pull system, produksi dipicu oleh konsumsi aktual di hilir (mis. kanban kosong), bukan oleh ramalan. Hasilnya inventori dan overproduksi berkurang.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Jadwal berbasis forecast dan material didorong saat siap: itu push system.\n• Membangun stok sebelum musim: strategi inventori (level), bukan pull.",11],
["One-piece flow means:","Moving products one at a time through the process steps","Producing a single product type on each line for the whole shift","Using one operator for the entire line","Inspecting one piece from each batch","One-piece flow memindahkan produk satu per satu dari langkah ke langkah tanpa menunggu batch, sehingga WIP dan lead time turun dan cacat cepat terdeteksi.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Satu jenis produk per shift: penjadwalan batch.\n• Satu operator untuk seluruh lini: tidak terkait.\n• Inspeksi satu sampel per batch: sampling mutu.",11],
["Which statement about a process in statistical control is true?","It can still be incapable of meeting specifications","It always meets customer specifications as well","It has no variation at all","It has a Cpk of at least 1.33","Proses yang in statistical control (stabil) hanya memiliki variasi common cause. Proses stabil tetap bisa tidak capable jika sebarannya lebih lebar dari spesifikasi atau rata-ratanya bergeser. Stabil tidak sama dengan mampu.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Selalu memenuhi spesifikasi: tidak; kapabilitas dinilai terpisah.\n• Tidak ada variasi: semua proses bervariasi.\n• Cpk ≥ 1,33: stabil tidak menjamin Cpk tinggi.",11],
["In a Gage R&R study, repeatability refers to variation:","When the same appraiser measures the same part repeatedly","Between different appraisers measuring the same part","Between different parts in the sample","Between measurements taken on different days","Dalam Gage R&R, repeatability (equipment variation) adalah variasi saat penilai yang sama mengukur part yang sama berulang kali dengan alat yang sama. Reproducibility (appraiser variation) adalah variasi antar penilai.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Antar penilai: reproducibility.\n• Antar part: part-to-part variation (yang seharusnya mendominasi).\n• Antar hari: stabilitas sistem ukur.",11],
["DMADV is used mainly to:","Design a new process or product","Improve an existing process","Control a process after improvement","Analyze the root cause of defects","DMADV (Define, Measure, Analyze, Design, Verify) dipakai untuk merancang proses atau produk baru, atau yang didesain ulang total (Design for Six Sigma).\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Memperbaiki proses yang ada: DMAIC.\n• Mengendalikan setelah perbaikan: fase Control DMAIC.\n• Menganalisis akar penyebab: fase Analyze.",11],
["In Six Sigma, a black belt typically:","Leads improvement projects, often full-time","Sponsors projects and provides resources","Supports projects part-time within their job","Sets the organization's quality strategy","Black belt memimpin proyek perbaikan Six Sigma, sering penuh waktu, dan membimbing green belt.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Sponsor yang menyediakan sumber daya: champion/sponsor.\n• Mendukung proyek paruh waktu: green belt (atau yellow belt).\n• Menetapkan strategi mutu: eksekutif dan master black belt membimbing program.",11],
["Integrity operating windows (IOWs) are:","Limits on process variables that, if exceeded, can damage equipment integrity","Time windows in which maintenance is permitted on running process equipment","Inspection ports used to view the inside of process vessels","Control chart limits used to monitor product quality","Integrity operating windows (IOW, API RP 584) adalah batas variabel proses (suhu, tekanan, pH, kandungan klorida) yang jika dilampaui dapat mempercepat kerusakan dan mengancam integritas peralatan.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Jendela waktu perawatan: tidak terkait.\n• Lubang inspeksi: itu inspection port/manway.\n• Control limit mutu: SPC untuk produk, bukan integritas peralatan.",13],
["Layers of protection analysis (LOPA) is used to:","Evaluate whether independent protection layers reduce risk enough","Identify process deviations by applying guide words to each node","Rank failure modes by their risk priority number","Calculate the reliability of a series system","LOPA (Layers of Protection Analysis) adalah metode semi-kuantitatif, biasanya setelah HAZOP, untuk menilai apakah lapisan proteksi independen (IPL) seperti alarm, SIS, dan relief valve cukup menurunkan risiko skenario ke level yang dapat diterima.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• Guide word per node: HAZOP.\n• Ranking dengan RPN: FMEA.\n• Reliabilitas sistem seri: analisis RBD.",13],
["The standard for safety instrumented systems in the process industry is:","IEC 61511","IEC 60812","ISO 14224","API 580","IEC 61511 adalah standar Safety Instrumented Systems (SIS) untuk industri proses, termasuk penentuan SIL (Safety Integrity Level). Induknya adalah IEC 61508.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• IEC 60812: FMEA.\n• ISO 14224: data keandalan dan taksonomi.\n• API 580: risk-based inspection.",13],
["Which OSHA PSM element covers inspection and testing of process equipment?","Mechanical integrity","Process hazard analysis","Management of change","Operating procedures","Elemen mechanical integrity dalam PSM mencakup prosedur tertulis, pelatihan, inspeksi dan pengujian, serta penanganan defisiensi untuk peralatan proses seperti bejana tekan, tangki, pipa, relief valve, sistem shutdown darurat, dan kontrol.\n\nMengapa pilihan lain kurang tepat:\n• PHA: identifikasi bahaya proses.\n• MOC: pengelolaan perubahan.\n• Operating procedures: instruksi operasi.",13]
];
